{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01307","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01307@rel:R19-11#1269343c","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01307","release":"R19-11","content":"supportsMultipleInstantiation vs. canBeInvoked- Concurrently The semantics of combining the attributes supportsMultiple- Instantiation and canBeInvokedConcurrently is summarized in Table 7.6.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_TPS_SoftwareComponentTemplate.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:25+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01307@rel:R20-11#1269343c","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01307","release":"R20-11","content":"supportsMultipleInstantiation vs. canBeInvoked- Concurrently The semantics of combining the attributes supportsMultiple- Instantiation and canBeInvokedConcurrently is summarized in Table 7.6.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_TPS_SoftwareComponentTemplate.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:45+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01307@rel:R25-11#adc53715","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01307","release":"R25-11","content":"Semantics of combining supportsMultipleInstantia- tion and canBeInvokedConcurrently supportsMultipleIn- stantiation canBeInvokedCon- currently Implication for an implementation of a RunnableEntity false false This implies that the implementation of the RunnableEntity will never be invoked concurrently from several tasks. The implementation does not need to care about reentrancy issues and can typically use static variables to store state. true false In case there are several instances of the same AtomicSwComponentType on the local ECU, the implementation of the RunnableEntity can still be invoked concurrently from several tasks. However, there will be no concurrent invocations of the implementation with the same instance handle . To ensure that this is safe, the implementation will typically use per-instance memory. true true In this case the RunnableEntity can be invoked concurrently from several tasks, even with the same instance handle.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_CP_TPS_SoftwareComponentTemplate.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T09:59:18+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01307","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R19-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R18-10"],"platform_releases":["R18-10","R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"requirement","name":"","module":"SWCT","cluster":"","page":"","doc_type":"TPS","ai":false,"first":"R19-11","last":"R25-11","changed":["R25-11"],"distinct":2},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-1cde9b4e3d0a1e32","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_RTE","p":95,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Combining supportsMultipleInstantiation and canBeInvokedConcurrently","n":7,"cap":"Figure 4.5: Software-component runnable entity, wait points and RTE Events","sha":"1cde9b4e3d0a1e322bb8b3d74c84fa1c6f89df615913aec6a8c13a6789de7119","nser":9,"src":"figure"},{"id":"FIG-721a33564d49ea41","doc":"AUTOSAR_SoftwareComponentTemplate","p":223,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"supportsMultipleInstantiation and canBeInvokedConcurrently semantics","n":3,"cap":"Figure 45: CalprmElementPrototypes in internal behavior","sha":"721a33564d49ea41a5b382c2ab00e828942ee62f1c4ade959b037c1677714762","nser":4,"src":"figure"},{"id":"FIG-90e94cbd1656a6eb","doc":"AUTOSAR_SoftwareComponentTemplate","p":175,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"InternalBehavior supportsMultipleInstantiation and canBeInvokedConcurrently","n":6,"cap":"Figure 93: Stack Memory Consumption","sha":"90e94cbd1656a6eb1fd026fc3ea5bb553d0af528ffca51fcf32df58bc5343f98","nser":1,"src":"fig